                        <forename>Josiah</forename>
                        <surname>Wedgwood</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1730-07-12">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1795-01-03"/>
                    <occupation>master potter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin established a friendship with the 
    Wedgwood family, including the potter Josiah (1730–1795) and  two of his surviving sons, 
    <persName key="WED03">Josiah II</persName> and <persName key="WED02">Thomas</persName> (1771–1805). For full details see entry on Thomas.  The evidence suggests 
    that most of the contact with the family was through Thomas, until his death in 1805, when 
    Josiah jr., becomes the sole point of contact - Josiah Sr (this person) having died in 1795.</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
